cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "annotation_st: config-driven cell annotation for Xenium spatial transcriptomics"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that turns a documented cell-annotation workflow for imaging-based
  spatial transcriptomics (coarse lineages per cluster, cancer-associated fibroblast
  subtypes, cancer stem-like cells, two-level immune subtypes, neighbourhood statistics)
  into a configurable, reproducible pipeline: opt-in marker sets with a referenced default
  library, per-stage provenance and staleness tracking, a hierarchical colour scheme that
  carries across figures and datasets, and interoperability with spatioloji_s.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ji"
    family-names: "Wang"
    email: "gynecoloji@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3443-5857"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/Annotation_st"
url: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/Annotation_st"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - Xenium
  - cell type annotation
  - marker genes
  - ovarian cancer
  - bioinformatics
# `version` + `date-released` are bumped automatically by release-please on each
# release (via the annotations below) — do not edit them by hand.
version: "0.1.0" # x-release-please-version
date-released: "2026-10-07" # x-release-please-date
